{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Statutory NHS passports for all children & young adults who are disabled",
        "additional_details": "Parents of disabled children and young adults are repeatedly asked to retell their child\u2019s full medical history at every appointment. This can be exhausting & retraumatising, and lead to inconsistent care. This new system should ensure professionals have immediate, accurate information \u2014 reducing repetition and improving care. No parent should have to relive their child\u2019s entire medical journey at each & every appointment.",
        "background": "We are calling for a national statutory Health & Needs Passport, available in both digital and paper formats. The digital version would be accessible across the NHS, and the paper version would provide a quick access summary with a QR code linking to the full medical record.",
